+Before reporting a candidate, trace the complete path from its source or
+state through the actual dispatch branch and helpers to the operation that
+causes the claimed impact. Check relevant caller, framework, and transport
+contracts instead of assuming they provide a guarantee. Separate reachability
+from impact, cite the line of the unchecked use or state transition, and
+choose a category that matches the operation. A nearby flaw or similar issue
+in another branch is not evidence for this candidate. Include lifecycle,
+concurrency, and error-path issues when they have plausible security impact,
+even without direct attacker-controlled bytes flowing to a sink.
+
