+  BOUNDS & PARSING — HIGH VALUE:
+  - At each read or copy, validate the length against the exact pointer and
+    span used there. For subregions and nested records, validate the starting
+    offset, complete header, and declared length against the remaining buffer
+    before forming pointers, reading, or advancing.
+  - Recheck bounds after cursor or index advances, on continuation and error
+    paths, and in the exact dispatch branch and helper reached. An enclosing
+    length check or a guard in a similar parser may not cover later accesses.
+  - Trace length and count values to their trust source; compare them with
+    both the source allocation and destination capacity, including prefixes
+    and offsets. Check arithmetic before using its result, as well as returned
+    counts, special-case branches, and runtime configuration updates.
+  - Check index domains before bitmap or mask operations. Track which bytes
+    are initialized and valid before parsing or exporting them, and whether
+    pointers remain valid after operations that can relocate their storage.
+
+  LIFETIME, CONCURRENCY & STATE — HIGH VALUE:
+  - Trace ownership and references through success, failure, timeout, retry,
+    rollback, close, removal, and asynchronous completion. Confirm that work
+    has stopped and every alias or child object remains alive before use or
+    reclamation; a related owner reference or removal from an index alone may
+    not protect it.
+  - Follow locks through callers and callees. Check that the lock protecting
+    shared state spans the whole access, and inspect nested acquisition order,
+    callbacks, synchronous waits or cancellation, and process/interrupt
+    context for deadlocks or races.
+  - Trace fields and invariants from every initialization path through
+    publication, callbacks, state transitions, and cleanup. Check partial
+    setup and unwind paths, work skipped before state updates, and values
+    reused after locks are released or shared state is rebuilt.
+  - Check validation order before side effects. For errors, warnings, and
+    assertions, trace reachability and what happens next: clean rejection is
+    usually not a finding, but a reachable fatal failure or continued mutation
+    of invalid shared state can be security-relevant.
+
   INJECTION & CODE EXECUTION — HIGH VALUE:
   - SQL / command / LDAP / XPath / NoSQL / template injection
   - path traversal in file operations
